<title>USA: Bank of Boston to consolidate 65 branches.</title>
<headline>Bank of Boston to consolidate 65 branches.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Boston Corp Friday said it will consolidate 65 of its Bank of Boston and BayBank branch offices into its network of 356 remaining branches when the banks merge and convert to a common operating system this year.</p>
<p>The company expects that about 400 branch employees will have opportunities in the new BankBoston organization, and branches will remain in 50 of the 51 towns where the consolidations are taking place.</p>
</text>
